From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SuperLeiyan <5438286+SuperLeiyan@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 00:41:48 +1030
Subject: [PATCH] PC5: the media parser's read requests are answered once, at
 their own offset (Wine patch 0491)

The parser's read request stayed posted after the frontend's read thread
answered it, so a read thread that came back before the demuxer took the
data read the same offset again, and that data answered the demuxer's next
request, at another offset. A WebM movie's demuxer then resynchronised and
skipped seconds of packets at a time. Each request is now given out once.
